# TypeScript sources. The eslint config parses with @babel/eslint-parser, which
# has no TypeScript plugin, so pointing eslint at a .ts/.tsx file is a parsing
# error. `eslint .` does not pick these up on its own (eslint 8 only walks .js),
# but this makes the exclusion explicit for direct paths and lint-staged.
# Type and syntax checking for these files comes from `npm run typecheck` (tsc).
# Revisit when the migration is far enough along to justify typescript-eslint.
*.ts
*.tsx

